.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-actions - Scan GitHub Actions workflows for supply-chain risks


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis actions [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
actions scans .github/workflows/*.yml for known risky patterns:
.IP \(bu 2
unpinned action refs (tag/branch instead of commit SHA)
.IP \(bu 2
suspicious run-script bodies (curl|sh, base64 decode, raw IPs)
.IP \(bu 2
pull_request_target jobs that check out PR code
.IP \(bu 2
permissions: write-all
.IP \(bu 2
attacker-controlled GitHub-context interpolation in run scripts

.PP
This is heuristic, not exhaustive — designed to catch the patterns
behind real-world incidents (tj-actions/changed-files 2025-03 etc).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for actions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis(1)\fP, \fBaegis-actions-scan(1)\fP
